# CueRCode - Project Brief

> **Project:** CueRCode - Professional QR Code Generator
> **Organisation:** MWBM Partners Ltd
> **Copyright:** 2025-present
> **Repository:** https://github.com/MWBMPartners/CueRCode
> **Primary Domain:** CueRCode.net
> **Secondary Domain:** CueRCode.me (redirects to CueRCode.net)
> **Tertiary Domain:** QRmy.Link (redirects to CueRCode.net with web link QR function)

---

## 1. Project Overview

CueRCode is a web-based service for generating customisable, downloadable QR codes. It provides both a fully responsive web UI and a RESTful API. The web frontend is itself an implementation built on top of the API, ensuring complete feature parity between the two interfaces.

---

## 2. QR Code Types

All standard QR code use cases must be supported, including but not limited to:

### 2.1 Web & Links

- **URL/Web Link** - with future integration with Go2My.Link URL shortener for dynamic links (keeping the QR code static while changing the destination)
- **App Store Links** - Apple App Store, Google Play Store, Amazon Appstore

### 2.2 Communication

- **Plain Text** - arbitrary text content
- **Email** - recipient address, subject, and body (mailto: scheme)
- **Phone Call** - phone number with country code (tel: scheme)
- **SMS Message** - recipient phone number with country code and message body (smsto: scheme)
- **WhatsApp Message** - recipient country code, phone number, and message
- **Zoom Meeting** - Meeting ID and hashed/unhashed password/passcode, or direct Zoom Meeting link

### 2.3 Contact & Calendar

- **vCard (Business Card)** - vCard 2.1, 3.0, and 4.0 support
- **Calendar Event** - iCal/vEvent format for diary invites/events

### 2.4 Payments

- **PayPal** - payment link
- **Bitcoin** - wallet address, amount in BTC, item name, and message

### 2.5 Media

- **MP3 File/Link**
- **Video File/Link**
- **PDF File/Link**
- **Image File/Link**
- **YouTube Link**

### 2.6 Social Media

- **Facebook** - Page, Profile, or Event link
- **Facebook Messenger** - direct message link
- **LinkedIn** - profile URL
- **Instagram** - profile link
- **Other platforms** as needed

### 2.7 Utility

- **Wi-Fi** - SSID network name, encryption type (WEP/WPA/WPA2/nopass), password, hidden network flag
- **Geolocation** - coordinates (uses native mapping app with Google Maps fallback), or Google Maps URL
- **Rating/Review** - link to rating/review page

---

## 3. Output Formats

QR codes must be available in the following image formats:

| Format | Transparency | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **SVG** | Alpha | Vector format, preferred for scalability |
| **PNG** | Alpha | Default raster format |
| **GIF** | Binary | Legacy transparency support |
| **JPG** | None | Lossy compression |
| **WEBP** | Alpha | Modern format |
| **JPEG XL** | Alpha | Next-generation format |
| **PDF** | N/A | Document format via FPDF/DOMPDF |

---

## 4. QR Code Customisation

Users must be able to customise the following aspects of generated QR codes:

### 4.1 Colours

- Foreground colour: solid, gradient, or image-based
- Background colour: transparent (default for formats supporting it), solid, gradient, or image-based

### 4.2 Design

- Multiple QR pattern/module designs
- Marker border/corner element shapes
- Marker centre shapes with custom colours

### 4.3 Logo/Centre Image

- Predefined set of logos (popular platforms, emoji, FontAwesome icons)
- Custom uploaded image
- Registered users can save their own logos for reuse

### 4.4 Frames

- Customisable frame styles (8+ styles)
- Frame label text
- Typeface selection for labels (Google Fonts and other free font libraries)

### 4.5 Technical Options

- Error correction level (L/M/Q/H) - defaults to recommended settings
- Output size (pixels)
- QR code precision/version selection
- Quiet zone (border) toggle

---

## 5. User Accounts & Organisations

### 5.1 Account Types

- **Individual User** - create, save, re-download, and modify QR codes
- **Organisation Account** - company-level QR code management as a premium service

### 5.2 Organisation Roles

- **Global Admin** - creates the organisation; manages all users, domains, subscriptions, payments, SSO configuration
- **Admin** - elevated privileges but fewer than Global Admin; can invite new members via tokenised email links
- **Regular User** - can create QR codes; modification permissions are configurable by admins

### 5.3 Authentication Methods

- **Local Accounts** (primary, initial implementation)
  - Password hashing with Argon2id
  - WebAuthn/Passkey support: Windows Hello, Touch ID (Fingerprint), Face ID (Facial Recognition)
- **SSO/OAuth Integration** (configurable by Organisation Global Admin):
  - Microsoft 365 (work/school accounts)
  - Google Workspace
  - Apple Account
  - Facebook/Instagram
  - Self-hosted WordPress
  - All SSO accounts MUST be linked to a local/internal account
  - Support for linking multiple corporate provider accounts
- **SIGNula Integration** (future) - link local accounts to SIGNula via API when available (https://github.com/MWBMPartners/SIGNula.id)

---

## 6. RESTful API

### 6.1 Functionality

- Create QR codes (with all customisation features)
- Preview QR codes (quick PNG preview without database save)
- Download QR codes (by UUID, with Content-Disposition headers)
- List supported QR types and output formats
- Save QR codes to user account (authenticated users only)
- Manage/modify existing QR codes (authenticated users only)
- Health check endpoint

### 6.2 Security

- API key authentication (HMAC-SHA256 hashed, timing-safe comparison)
- CSRF token support for web UI AJAX requests
- Anonymous fallback for basic generation
- Rate limiting (per-minute and per-day windows via tblAPIRateLog)

### 6.3 Response Formats

- **JSON** (default) - with associated JSON schema for validation
- **XML** - structured with embedded XSLT for browser viewing

### 6.4 Documentation

- Swagger/OpenAPI 3.0 specification
- Interactive Swagger UI at `/api/docs/`
- PHP file extensions hidden from all API endpoints (directory-based routing)

---

## 7. Tech Stack

### 7.1 Backend

| Component | Specification |
| --- | --- |
| **Language** | PHP 8.5 (target) with backward compatibility to PHP 8.4 |
| **Database** | MySQL via MySQLi only (prepared statements for ALL queries) |
| **Encryption** | AES-256-GCM with HKDF key derivation and salt |
| **Password Hashing** | Argon2id via `password_hash()` |
| **QR Library** | chillerlan/php-qrcode v5.x (self-hosted, no Composer) |
| **PDF Library** | FPDF v1.86 (self-hosted) |
| **Email** | Microsoft Graph API via M365 shared mailbox (DKIM/DMARC compliant) |

### 7.2 Frontend

| Component | Specification |
| --- | --- |
| **Markup** | HTML5, fully compliant, responsive |
| **Styling** | CSS3+ with modern features and animations |
| **Framework** | Bootstrap 5.3+ (CDN with local fallback) |
| **Icons** | FontAwesome 6+ (CDN with local fallback), SVG-first |
| **JavaScript** | jQuery 3.7+ (CDN with local fallback), AJAX with graceful fallback |
| **Fonts** | Google Fonts for frame label typefaces |

### 7.3 Bot Protection (priority order, based on available API keys)

1. Cloudflare Turnstile
2. reCAPTCHA
3. hCaptcha

---

## 8. PHP Coding Standards

- **Platform Neutrality:** Use PHP predefined constants everywhere (`DIRECTORY_SEPARATOR`, `PHP_EOL`, `__FILE__`, `dirname()`, etc.)
- **Full Notation:** Always use full multi-line notation for code blocks (if/else, loops, etc.) - no shorthand
- **Indentation:** Properly indented with detailed inline comments and comment blocks
- **Comments:** Include reference links to official documentation where applicable; emojis welcome in comments
- **Modularity:** Minimise duplication via `require_once`, `include_once` with existence checks and error handling
- **Debug Mode:** URL parameter switches (`?debug=true`, `?dev=true`) for detailed error visibility
- **Error Logging:** All PHP errors/warnings/notices logged to `tblErrorLog` with severity, error code, title, detail, backtrace, request URL, and headers
- **Activity Logging:** All application activity logged to `tblActivityLog`
- **Security:** All user inputs sanitised; sensitive values encrypted with salt before database storage

---

## 9. Database Standards

- **Connection:** MySQLi only, singleton pattern
- **Queries:** Prepared statements for ALL SQL executed in PHP
- **Naming:** Tables use `tbl` prefix with PascalCase; columns use camelCase
- **Settings:** All config stored in `tblSettings` (except DB connection credentials)
- **Sensitive Data:** Values marked `isSensitive` are AES-256-GCM encrypted with HKDF-derived keys and random salt
- **Engine:** InnoDB with `utf8mb4_unicode_ci` collation

---

## 10. Directory Structure

```text
web/
├── _auth_keys/                     ← Server-wide credentials (outside web root)
│   └── auth_creds.php              ← DB creds, API keys (never web-accessible)
├── _includes/                      ← Server-wide shared includes
├── _functions/                     ← Server-wide shared functions
├── _libraries/                     ← Server-wide shared libraries
├── _uploads/                       ← Server-wide uploads
├── _backups/                       ← Server-wide backups
└── CueRCode.net/                   ← Main website
    ├── _auth_keys/                 ← Site-specific credentials
    ├── _includes/                  ← Site-specific includes (bootstrap.php, SQL, templates)
    ├── _functions/                 ← Site-specific functions (QR engine, API handlers)
    ├── _libraries/                 ← Third-party PHP libraries (chillerlan, FPDF)
    ├── _uploads/                   ← User uploads (logos, generated QR codes)
    ├── _backups/                   ← Site backups
    ├── public_html/                ← Production web root
    ├── public_html_dev_alpha/      ← Alpha development (restricted access)
    ├── public_html_dev_beta/       ← Beta development (restricted access)
    ├── public_html_landing/        ← Pre-launch landing page
    └── public_html_redir/          ← Redirection web root
```

**Key Rules:**
- Directories prefixed with `_` (underscore) are private, secured via `.htaccess` deny-all rules
- Only `public_html*` directories are web-accessible
- `auth_creds.php` files must never echo/return data if accessed directly; should redirect to main site
- Third-party libraries that cannot be referenced via CDN must be manually downloaded and placed in `_libraries/`

---

## 11. Web UI Requirements

### 11.1 Responsiveness

- Fully responsive across all devices: desktop monitors, smart TVs, tablets, phones
- Support all screen DPI resolutions, orientations, and aspect ratios
- High-density and HDR display support
- No `<table>` tags for layout purposes

### 11.2 Accessibility

- WCAG 2.1 AA compliant
- Colourblind-friendly UI toggle
- Screen reader support with proper ARIA attributes
- Skip-to-main-content links
- `prefers-reduced-motion` media queries for animations
- Focus-visible indicators

### 11.3 Display Modes

- Dark/Light mode with system preference detection (`prefers-color-scheme`)
- Manual toggle to override system setting

### 11.4 Logged-In User Display

- Top-right corner user indicator showing:
  - User avatar (priority: local custom > MS365/Google > Gravatar > default placeholder)
  - User name
  - Dropdown menu for profile settings

### 11.5 Progressive Enhancement

- AJAX for dynamic content loading (avoid full page refreshes)
- Graceful fallback when JavaScript is unavailable
- PWA support (service worker, offline fallback page, manifest.json)
- SVG-first graphics with PNG/APNG fallback (only load fallback if SVG unsupported)

### 11.6 Form Standards

- Dynamic field validation on all forms
- Datepickers for consistent date format
- Bot protection (Cloudflare Turnstile / reCAPTCHA / hCaptcha) when API keys are available
- PHP file extensions hidden from all URLs

