## 18. Documentation Standards

The following files must be maintained throughout development:

| File | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `README.md` | Project overview, setup instructions, tech stack |
| `CHANGELOG.md` | Keep a Changelog format with Semantic Versioning |
| `PROJECT_STATUS.md` | Phase-by-phase build progress tracking |
| `DEV_NOTES.md` | Technical decisions, coding standards, constraints |
| `.claude/` | Claude AI memory, context, and prompts |
| Swagger/OpenAPI | API documentation (`openapi.json`) |

---

## 19. Standing Instructions (Per-Prompt Checklist)

After every prompt/action, complete the following **in this order**:

1. Update `CHANGELOG.md`, `README.md`, `PROJECT_STATUS.md`, `DEV_NOTES.md`
2. Update GitHub Issues - track implemented features, applied fixes
3. Update GitHub Project tracking
4. Update GitHub Milestones tracking
5. Update GitHub Wiki
6. Update Swagger/OpenAPI documentation
7. Run thorough lint/syntax checks, fixing ALL issues (warnings, notifications, errors)
8. Run thorough security checks, applying all suggested fixes
9. Update `.gitignore` as needed
10. COMMIT changes (**DO NOT PUSH** - push is done manually)
11. Update `.claude/` memory, context, and prompts

---

## 20. Code Quality Standards

- All code (PHP, JavaScript, CSS, SQL) must be fully commented/annotated in detail
- Proper indentation throughout (code can be minified for deployment, but source must be readable)
- Emojis are welcome in code comments to visually call out sections
- Zero lint/syntax/security warnings - all issues must be resolved before commit
- Version numbering embedded in commented code blocks in each file
